    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is headlined today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.21), who stands as our most productive asset against Rocker. With a favorable platoon advantage and a projected leadoff spot, **Gunnar Henderson** occupies the highest efficiency ceiling on the roster. He is closely followed by **Kyle Tucker** (75.28), **Andy Pages** (74.43), and **Jackson Merrill** (74.20), all of whom benefit significantly from facing weak SP_xERA matchups above 4.80. Specifically, **Andy Pages** and **Jackson Merrill** are primed to exploit high-variance pitching, with the former aided by a slow opposing delivery that enhances his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor for our internal scarcity model. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) also warrants attention; he offers the best SP_xERA leverage of the group, with his projection buoyed by a 15% skill boost against Holmes and a strong dynamic platoon edge.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo**, whose 45.68 efficiency score fell just outside the starting rotation. While **Coby Mayo** possesses latent power, the optimizer penalized his projected #7 spot in the lineup and a negative platoon split against Rocker, ultimately preferring the higher-floor utility of **Nasim Nunez** (58.06). Meanwhile, we are tracking a 39% rain risk for **Miguel Vargas** (54.52) in his matchup against Cantillo. While **Miguel Vargas** remains a viable start, his value is slightly depressed by the presence of an elite defensive catcher and the weather threat; should the rain risk materialize, we will look to pivot to our bench assets. Finally, users should monitor the status of **Liam Hicks**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Kyle Tucker**, as their high-end projections are currently contingent on unconfirmed lineups. Should these players shift lower in their respective batting orders, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation.",
